summary:
  Every picture is read with a box to be cropped to, which enlarges a
  small raster while it is read.

history:
  Asked to crop or fit, Qt scales a picture to the source size as it
  decodes it (Qt 6.12: a PNG of 32 by 32 came back 600 by 600). After that
  nothing can tell a small logo from a cover, and the larger view cannot
  stop at twice its pixels. Only a drawing is cropped to a box, one of its
  own shape; a raster is read as it is. This mutant crops every picture
  that has no box of its own to the whole source size.

target:
  package/contents/ui/CoverImage.qml

find:
          // With a box of the drawing's own shape, cropping to it scales the
          // drawing to the box and cuts nothing.
          fillMode: cover._box.width > 0 ? Image.PreserveAspectCrop : Image.Stretch

replace:
          // With a box of the drawing's own shape, cropping to it scales the
          // drawing to the box and cuts nothing.
          fillMode: cover._box.width > 0 ? Image.PreserveAspectCrop : Image.PreserveAspectCrop

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cover_larger_fetch.py::test_the_larger_cover_is_the_picture_the_page_already_holds,
  which runs first and finds the picture of 400 pixels read at 600, and behind it by
  tests/qml/tst_coverimage.qml::test_a_raster_says_its_own_size_and_covers_the_frame.
  Line-neutral.
